  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Board identity: the image is titled 'LoRa-E5 Dev Board Pinout' (module LoRa-E5-HF); the record is 'Wio-E5 Development Kit'. The image does not itself show that these are the same product.",
    "Top header has an empty slot (no pad drawn) between D5/PB5 and GND, and the bottom header has one between A3/PB3 and A4/PB4; each strip is recorded as one connector without a position for the empty slot. Whether the slot is a physical hole (and whether each strip is one header or two) is not settled by the image."
  ],
  "notes": "Top/bottom header labels use the grey MCU port names (PA10, PB14...) as label per rule 5, with silkscreen/board names (MOSI, D0, TX2...) in functions; where no port name is printed (5V, 3V3, GND, RST) the silkscreen name is the label and the coloured tag (e.g. '5V (EN)', 'MCU_VCC') is in functions. Position 3 on the bottom header is printed 'SWDLK' (bottom header silkscreen and tag) while the blue SWD/SWIM header silkscreen prints 'SWCLK'; both recorded as printed. Skipped: two-pin jumpers (Power Test Pin, RS485 Enable(A4), Button Enable(D0), LED Enable(D5), 3V3 Enable(D9), 5V Enable(D10)) whose individual pins are not labeled, USB-C, antenna (SMA/u.FL), buttons, LEDs. Battery JST connector included because its pins are marked + and -."
